      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T18:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SkRasterClip::isRect() only returns true if the clip is rectangular AND lies on pixel boundary, so whether or not fIsBW is true, it can still be represented as an SkIRect or an SkRegion (in this case). So an original AA rect with fractional coverage on some edges would never get into this optimization and we just call op() on line 215.",
